# Line endings are normalised on commit and checked out as LF everywhere.
#
# This is here because 33 files on this branch reached the repository with CRLF,
# carried in one at a time by copies from a Windows machine. Python, git and
# markdown all tolerate it, so it accumulated silently for months. Two things
# do not tolerate it: bash refuses a script outright at its first function
# definition, and Python's csv module treats a lone CR as a record separator --
# which had silently split results/governor_joint_degradation.csv into seven
# rows and hidden its last column from every reader.
#
# text=auto lets git detect binaries rather than listing them.
* text=auto eol=lf
